t":195,"end":195,"description":"a peptide antigen"},{"type":"Region","start":207,"end":298,"description":"Alpha-3"},{"type":"Domain","start":209,"end":295,"description":"Ig-like C1-type"},{"type":"Disulfide bond","start":227,"end":283,"description":""},{"type":"Region","start":299,"end":308,"description":"Connecting peptide"},{"type":"Transmembrane","start":309,"end":332,"description":"Helical"},{"type":"Topological domain","start":333,"end":365,"description":"Cytoplasmic"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":343,"end":343,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":344,"end":344,"description":"Phosphotyrosine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":349,"end":349,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":350,"end":350,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":352,"end":352,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":356,"end":356,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":359,"end":359,"description":"Phosphoserine"}],"interfaces":{"B2M":[30,32,33,34,36,47,49,51,56,59,72,109,110,111,118,120,121,122,139,140,141,142,143,144,145,146,161,216,226,228,230,255,256,257,258,259,260,261,262,266,268]},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Heterotrimer that consists of an alpha chain HLA-A, a beta chain B2M and a peptide (peptide-HLA-A-B2M) (PubMed:11502003, PubMed:18275829, PubMed:19177349, PubMed:19542454, PubMed:21943705, PubMed:22245737, PubMed:24395804, PubMed:26758806, PubMed:28250417, PubMed:7504010, PubMed:7506728, PubMed:7679507, PubMed:7694806, PubMed:7935798, PubMed:8805302, PubMed:8906788, PubMed:9177355). Early in biogenesis, HLA-A-B2M dimer interacts with the components of the peptide-loading complex composed of TAPBP, TAP1-TAP2, TAPBPL, PDIA3/ERP57 and CALR (PubMed:21263072). Interacts with TAP1-TAP2 transporter via TAPBP; this interaction is obligatory for the loading of peptide epitopes delivered to the ER by TAP1-TAP2 transporter (PubMed:21263072, PubMed:8630735, PubMed:8805302). Interacts with TAPBPL; TAPBPL binds peptide-free HLA-A-B2M complexes or those loaded with low affinity peptides, likely facilitating peptide exchange for higher affinity peptides (PubMed:26869717, PubMed:35725941). Only optimally assembled peptide-HLA-B2M trimer translocates to the surface of antigen-presenting cells, where it interacts with TCR and CD8 coreceptor on the surface of T cells. HLA-A (via polymorphic alpha-1 and alpha-2 domains) interacts with antigen-specific TCR (via CDR3 domains) (PubMed:12796775, PubMed:18275829, PubMed:22245737). One HLA-A molecule (mainly via nonpolymorphic alpha-3 domain) interacts with one CD8A homodimer (via CDR-like loop); this interaction ensures peptide-HLA-A-B2M recognition by CD8-positive T cells only (PubMed:2784196, PubMed:9177355). Alleles A*23:01; A*24:02 and A*32:01 interact (via Bw4 motif) with KIR3DL1 on NK cells; this interaction is direct"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with HHV-8 MIR1 protein"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with HTLV-1 accessory protein p12I"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"P04439-2","name":"2","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":371,"transcripts":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,175],[188,188,150],[344,338,28]],"edits":[{"start":176,"end":187,"original":"EAEQLRAYLDGT","replacement":"AAEQQRAYLEGR","added":12},{"start":337,"end":337,"original":"S","replacement":"SGGEGVK","added":7}],"missing":0,"replaced":12,"novel":18,"foldedAbsent":12,"foldedMissing":0,"features":[[3,0,12],[9,0,12],[14,0,1],[15,0,1]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-P04439-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P04439-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":86.4,"plddt":[[0,5],[50,1],[0,4],[50,4],[0,8],[50,2],[70,1],[90,273],[70,1],[50,2],[0,4],[50,4],[70,24],[50,4],[0,24],[50,1],[0,4],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1]],"losingConfidence":0}}],"ensemblGenes":["ENSG00